TypeScript Lesson 11: Union Types & Type Narrowing 🚀
Aaj hum seekhenge ki ek variable mein multiple types allow kaise karte hain aur TypeScript ko kaise batate hain ki abhi variable mein kaunsa type ka data hai.
1. Union Type kya hota hai?
Maan lo ek variable mein kabhi number aur kabhi string store karna hai.
let data: string | number;

data = 100;       // Valid
data = "Hello";   // Valid

console.log(data);


Yahan | ka matlab hai OR.
- string | number = string OR number.
- string | number | boolean = string OR number OR boolean.
Memory trick: | ko OR samjho.
2. Union Type ki zaroorat kyun hai?
Maan lo user ka ID number bhi ho sakta hai aur string bhi.
let userId: string | number;

userId = 101;
userId = "USER101";


Dono valid hain.
Lekin ye invalid hoga:
userId = true; // TypeScript error


Kyunki boolean allowed types mein nahi hai.
3. Type Narrowing kya hai?
Maan lo variable string | number hai. Ab tum us par string wala method .toUpperCase() use karna chahte ho.
Direct use karoge to TypeScript error de sakta hai, kyunki variable number bhi ho sakta hai.
Solution: pehle type check karo.
function printData(data: string | number): void {
    if (typeof data === "string") {
        console.log(data.toUpperCase());
    } else {
        console.log(data * 2);
    }
}

printData("hello");
printData(10);


Output:
HELLO
20


Samjho:
- typeof data === "string" check karta hai ki data string hai ya nahi.
- if ke andar TypeScript jaanta hai ki data string hai.
- else ke andar yahan data number hoga.
Isi ko Type Narrowing kehte hain: possible types ko check karke ek specific type tak narrow karna.
4. Union Type ke saath conditions
function showId(id: string | number): void {
    if (typeof id === "number") {
        console.log("ID doubled:", id * 2);
    } else {
        console.log("ID:", id.toUpperCase());
    }
}

showId(25);
showId("abc123");


Output:
ID doubled: 50
ID: ABC123


5. Literal Union Types
Kabhi-kabhi hum sirf kuch fixed values allow karna chahte hain.
type OrderStatus = "pending" | "shipped" | "delivered";

let status: OrderStatus = "pending";

status = "shipped";   // Valid
status = "cancelled"; // Error


Yahan OrderStatus string ka koi bhi value accept nahi karega. Sirf diye gaye 3 options valid hain.
Real projects mein ye orders, payment status, user roles aur application status ke liye useful hai.

